1768 0 obj
<</Title(\200 4 wild-caught salmon fillets \200 2 cups baby potatoes, quartered \200 2 cups green beans or asparagus \200 2-3 tbsp olive oil \200 3 cloves garlic, minced \200 Zest + juice of 1 lemon \200 Salt, pepper, and fresh dill)/Dest[33 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1762 0 R>>
endobj

1769 0 obj
<</Title(01 Preheat oven to 400\260F. Toss potatoes with 1 tbsp oil, salt, and pepper; spread on a sheet pan. 02 Roast for 20 minutes, then push potatoes to one side. 03 Mix remaining oil with garlic, lemon zest, and juice. Coat salmon and vegetables. 04 Add salmon and green beans beside the potatoes; bake 10-15 more minutes. 05 Sprinkle with dill and serve.)/Dest[33 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1763 0 R>>
endobj

1770 0 obj
<</Title(\200 3 tbsp extra-virgin olive oil, divided \200 6 garlic cloves, thinly sliced and divided \200 4 cups broccoli florets \200 1/2 cup diced red bell pepper \200 1 lb peeled, deveined shrimp \200 2 tsp lemon juice + salt and pepper)/Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1766 0 R>>
endobj

1771 0 obj
<</Title(01 Heat 2 tbsp oil in a pot over medium heat. Saute half the garlic until golden, about 1 minute. 02 Add broccoli, bell pepper, salt, and pepper; cover and steam 3-5 minutes. Transfer to a bowl. 03 Add 1 tbsp oil and remaining garlic to the pot; cook until golden. 04 Add shrimp and seasoning; cook 3-5 minutes until opaque. 05 Return vegetables to the pot, stir in lemon juice, and serve. PRO TIP Serve over cauliflower rice, quinoa, or greens.)/Dest[32 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1767 0 R>>
endobj

